  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 220-10-45 and ASC 205-20-45, the income statement presents income from continuing operations first, followed by discontinued operations (net of tax) to arrive at net income. OCI is then presented either in a separate statement or below net income in a single continuous statement.
Wrong (A): Discontinued operations never precede continuing operations; continuing operations is always the starting point for income measurement.
