-- Q11592: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IAS 7.33, IFRS allows interest paid to be classified as either operating or financing. Under ASC 230-10-45-17, U.S. GAAP requires interest paid as operating. If Eurotech classifies interest paid as financing, a GAAP peer would include it in operating, making the GAAP entity''s operating cash flows appear lower by comparison.
Wrong (B): Dividends paid as financing is identical under both frameworks, so this classification creates no analytical difference.
Wrong (C): GAAP does not permit classifying interest paid as financing, so both classifications are not equally permitted.
Wrong (D): Under GAAP, interest paid must be operating, not financing, so the classification difference does create an analytical impact.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11592;

-- Q11595: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 320-10-35 and ASC 220-10-45, when AFS securities are sold, the previously unrealized gain in AOCI is reclassified into net income via a reclassification adjustment. Net income increases by $85,000 and OCI decreases by the same amount, so comprehensive income is unchanged.
Wrong (B): The reclassification adjustment simultaneously removes the $85,000 from OCI, preventing double-counting in comprehensive income.
Wrong (C): The reclassification does not remove the gain from equity entirely; it shifts the gain from AOCI to retained earnings through net income.
Wrong (D): Net income does increase upon sale, and OCI does decrease by the reclassification; both components change even though their sum remains constant.$EXPL$
