-- Q11604: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 230-10-45-17, interest paid is classified as an operating activity under U.S. GAAP, regardless of the source of the underlying debt. The FASB concluded that interest payments affect net income determination and thus belong in operations.
Wrong (A): Under U.S. GAAP, interest paid is never classified as financing despite its relationship to borrowing; GAAP mandates operating classification.
Wrong (B): IFRS allows interest paid to be classified as financing, but GAAP requires operating; the two frameworks differ on this point.
Wrong (C): Interest paid has no connection to investing activities; investing involves acquisitions and disposals of long-term assets and investments.$EXPL$
