-- Q11605: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): ASU 2015-17 (codified in ASC 740-10-45-4) requires all deferred tax assets and liabilities to be classified as noncurrent, regardless of when the underlying temporary differences are expected to reverse. The previous requirement to bifurcate into current and noncurrent portions was eliminated.
Wrong (A): This reflects the pre-ASU treatment that classified deferred taxes based on the reversal period of each temporary difference, which is no longer permitted.
Wrong (B): Classifying the entire amount as current contradicts ASU 2015-17, which mandates noncurrent classification for all deferred taxes.
Wrong (D): This combines the outdated bifurcation approach with an improper netting method; all deferred taxes are noncurrent under current guidance.$EXPL$
