-- Q11606: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 210-10-45-3, the operating cycle is the time it takes for a business to convert cash to inventory, sell the inventory, and collect cash from customers. When the operating cycle exceeds one year (as with aged whiskey), it replaces one year as the current/noncurrent threshold.
Wrong (B): The period between balance sheet dates describes the fiscal period, not the operating cycle; the operating cycle measures the cash-to-cash conversion timeline.
Wrong (C): Converting cash into investments describes investing activities, not the operating cycle of core business operations.
Wrong (D): The time to prepare and issue financial statements relates to the reporting process, not to the operational cash conversion cycle.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11606;

