  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 860-10-40, a transfer of receivables with recourse typically fails the sale criteria because the transferor retains effective control through the credit-loss obligation. The advance is therefore a secured borrowing classified as a financing activity under ASC 230-10-45-14, not an operating inflow.
Wrong (A): The recourse provision, not the underlying asset type, determines whether the cash flow is operating or financing; recourse prevents sale treatment.
Wrong (B): Not all factoring is financing; without recourse, a qualifying transfer can be treated as a sale with operating classification.
Wrong (D): The advance does not represent operating receivable collections because the transfer failed sale treatment and is a secured borrowing.$EXPL$
